## Harness honesty note

My first mutation kill-rule matched `/FAILED/i` anywhere in output and was fooled by a CONTRACT description containing the word *failed* (`run11`: "a failed head-count query"). It reported **0 survivors** — a vacuous mutation proof. Replaced with a baseline-differential rule, which found the 3 real survivors. Recorded in the committed README so it isn't repeated.

